            <ArticleTitle>Anomalous the Left Main Coronary Artery Originating from the Right Coronary Artery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e49-e50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1055/s-0034-1378128</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The coronary anomalies are rarely seen in clinical practice. A 47-year-old female patient presented to hospital with chest pain on exertion. The coronary angiography and cardiac tomography showed the anomalous origin of the left main from the right coronary artery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
